---
import CaseStudyLayout from '../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro';
import CouncilReplay from '../../components/ai-lab/CouncilReplay.astro';
import AskAiTranscript from '../../components/ai-lab/AskAiTranscript.astro';
import ExperimentIndex from '../../components/ai-lab/ExperimentIndex.astro';
import CompareSlider from '../../components/case/CompareSlider.astro';
import Figure from '../../components/case/Figure.astro';
import DisplayNumeral from '../../components/case/DisplayNumeral.astro';
import RuledList from '../../components/case/RuledList.astro';
import RuledRow from '../../components/case/RuledRow.astro';
import { awards, councilReplay, askAiExchange, auditSnapshot, lessons } from '../../data/aiLab';

const metrics = [
  { value: String(awards.length), label: 'Hackathon Awards' }
];
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  title="AI Lab"
  subtitle="How I work with AI: I let it widen the options, I make the call, and I build the checks that catch what it misses."
  description="How Hafsa Usmani designs with AI: a real AI design review and the call she made, the assistant on her site, an automated accessibility audit, and earlier AI experiments."
  heroImage="/images/ai-lab/hero.png"
  ogImage="/images/og/ai-lab.jpg"
  industry="AI / Design Tools"
  role="Product Designer"
  timeline="2025 - Ongoing"
  platforms="Web"
  tools={[]}
  metrics={metrics}
  prevProject={{
    title: 'HafsaUsmani.com',
    href: '/work/portfolio-website',
    subtitle: 'AI-assisted portfolio development'
  }}
  nextProject={{
    title: 'MedRec',
    href: '/work/medrec',
    subtitle: 'Streamlined diabetes management'
  }}
>
  <section class="case-section">
    <p class="lab-eyebrow">01 · Deciding with AI</p>
    <h2>Three AI reviewers disagreed. I made the call.</h2>
    <p>
      When I get feedback on a design, I ask AI reviewers with different jobs to argue it out: a hiring manager,
      an art director and an engineer. They give me more options and sharper objections than I'd get alone.
      Choosing between them is still my job. This is one real review from {councilReplay.date}.
    </p>
    <CouncilReplay />
    <Figure n={1} wide caption="The homepage hero before and after the call. Drag, or use the slider, to compare.">
      <CompareSlider
        before={councilReplay.before}
        after={councilReplay.after}
        width={1440}
        height={900}
        subject="the homepage hero"
        start={50}
      />
    </Figure>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section">
    <p class="lab-eyebrow">02 · Shipped on this site</p>
    <h2>An assistant that only answers from this site</h2>
    <p>
      Recruiters ask the same questions about every candidate. The assistant on this site answers them from
      my case studies and nothing else. When it doesn't know, it says so and points to my email.
    </p>
    <Figure n={2} wide caption={`Two real answers from the live assistant (${askAiExchange.model}), captured 4 November 2026. ${askAiExchange.stored}`}>
      <AskAiTranscript />
    </Figure>
    <p class="lab-try">
      <a href="/contact" data-ask-ai class="lab-try-link">Ask it something <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section">
    <p class="lab-eyebrow">03 · Checking the work</p>
    <h2>The scanner found {auditSnapshot.scanner.found} problems. I found {auditSnapshot.byHand.length}.</h2>
    <p>
      I wrote an audit script that runs every page of this site through axe-core at desktop and phone width,
      then checks it fits a 320px screen. It's fast and it never forgets a page. It also can't see colour over
      a gradient, so I check those by hand.
    </p>
    <div class="lab-tally">
      <DisplayNumeral value={String(auditSnapshot.scanner.found)} label="found by the scanner" note={`${auditSnapshot.pages} pages: ${auditSnapshot.scanner.scope}`} />
      <DisplayNumeral value={String(auditSnapshot.byHand.length)} label="found by hand" note="Both fixed before release" />
    </div>
    <RuledList label="Failures found by hand">
      {auditSnapshot.byHand.map((f) => (
        <RuledRow label={f.issue}>
          <p>{f.before}.</p>
          <p class="lab-fixed">{f.after}.</p>
        </RuledRow>
      ))}
    </RuledList>
    <p class="lab-after-list">
      The script lives in the site's repo and runs with <code>{auditSnapshot.command}</code>. The same habit
      shaped <a href="/work/philly-truce">Philly Truce</a>, where every contrast ratio on the page is computed
      in code and pinned by tests.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section">
    <p class="lab-eyebrow">04 · Experiments</p>
    <h2>Earlier AI builds</h2>
    <p>
      Builds with different AI tools, from quick experiments to full case studies. Two won awards.
    </p>
    <ExperimentIndex />
  </section>

  <section class="case-section">
    <p class="lab-eyebrow">05 · What I've learned</p>
    <h2>Two things I keep relearning</h2>
    <ol class="lab-lessons">
      {lessons.map((l) => <li>{l}</li>)}
    </ol>
  </section>
</CaseStudyLayout>

<style>
  /* The terminal's prompt marker follows the site accent, not the retired orange */
  :global(.case-content) {
    --terminal-accent: var(--color-accent-text);
  }

  /* Calmer rhythm: more air between chapters, no divider lines */
  :global(.case-content) .case-section {
    padding-bottom: 0;
    margin-bottom: clamp(88px, 10vw, 128px);
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  :global(.case-content) .case-section h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.2vw, 2.25rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  :global(.case-content) .lab-eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    font: 500 12px/1.4 var(--font-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-accent-text);
  }

  :global(.case-content) .lab-try {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .lab-try-link {
    font: 500 13px/1.5 var(--font-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-fg);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
    text-underline-offset: 0.3em;
  }

  .lab-try-link:hover { color: var(--color-accent-text); }

  .lab-tally {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem 2rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 720px) {
    .lab-tally { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  }

  :global(.case-content) .lab-fixed {
    color: var(--color-fg);
  }

  :global(.case-content) .lab-after-list {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  :global(.case-content) .lab-after-list code {
    font: 500 0.875em var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--color-fg);
  }

  /* Lessons: hanging numerals, lead-size sentences, no containers */
  .lab-lessons {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: lesson;
  }

  :global(.case-content) .lab-lessons li {
    position: relative;
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
    padding-left: 2.5rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.2vw, 1.5rem);
    line-height: 1.45;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--color-fg);
    counter-increment: lesson;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .lab-lessons li::before {
    content: counter(lesson);
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.1em;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1em;
    color: var(--color-accent-text);
  }

  @media (min-width: 1100px) {
    :global(.case-content) .lab-lessons li { padding-left: 0; }
    .lab-lessons li::before { left: -3rem; }
  }
</style>
